course: dictionary
lesson: 8988
title: What does situation mean?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A situation is everything that is happening at a certain time and place, and how things are right now. Think of it as the whole picture around you.
explain: Sometimes a situation is a problem or a tricky moment you have to deal with. «Knowing why something is dangerous helps you avoid it even in a new situation.» Here a new situation is a new time and place you have not been in before.
explain: Situation can also mean where something is placed, like the situation of a town. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: «Situation» means everything that is happening at a certain time and place, and how things are.
fact: «Situation» can mean a problem or a difficult moment you need to deal with.
fact: «Situation» can also mean where a building or town is placed.
fact: «Tricky situation» means a difficult moment, as in a story where a character must find a way out.
fact: Check the words around «situation» to decide which meaning fits, then swap your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «A thought experiment is an imagined situation used to test ideas.» What is a situation in this sentence? | *An imagined set of circumstances used to test ideas | A dull, boring lesson | A type of cloud | A sum of money
exercise: «Knowing why something is dangerous helps you avoid it even in a new situation.» What does new situation mean here? | A new game at school | *A new time and place you have not been in before | A new pair of shoes | A new word in a dictionary
exercise: «The situation of the town is on a hill above the river.» What does situation mean here? | A problem the town has | The number of people who live there | *Where the town is placed | The weather in the town
test: The fire alarm rang, and the teacher said, «The situation is under control.» What does situation mean? | A type of drill | A kind of fire engine | A school subject | *What is happening and how things are
test: «Knowing someone in a similar situation helps a child feel less alone.» What does situation mean here? | A map of a town | A kind of weather | A long test at school | *A tricky moment or problem like the one you have
exam: Which meaning of situation fits «a tricky situation» in a story? | A place on a map | A type of music | A kind of exercise | *A difficult moment or problem
